\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Per-circuit cold compute time of the native engine against PolyBoRi (left) and CUDD BDD (right), same minimal loop, all workloads, circuits completed by both. A constant factor over two orders of magnitude of running time is what a per-call cost would produce, which is why we calibrate the bindings separately. Solid: equal time; dotted: 4$\times $ faster.}}{8}{figure.1}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:scatter}{{1}{8}{Per-circuit cold compute time of the native engine against PolyBoRi (left) and CUDD BDD (right), same minimal loop, all workloads, circuits completed by both. A constant factor over two orders of magnitude of running time is what a per-call cost would produce, which is why we calibrate the bindings separately. Solid: equal time; dotted: 4$\times $ faster}{figure.1}{}}
